{"version":"1","id":"spring","handle":"spring","name":"Spring","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/t_logo,f_auto/v1/logos/spring","description":null,"is_squad":false,"x":-6.7557,"y":2.5013,"cluster_id":3,"posts_collected":598,"newest_post_at":"2026-03-18T00:00:00.000Z","oldest_post_at":"2020-09-17T22:31:00.000Z","features":{"hype_score":0.01087,"listicle_ratio":0.0,"question_ratio":0.001672,"avg_read_time":1.720736,"summary_length_avg":257.993311,"title_length_avg":50.118729,"title_length_var":470.489248,"tag_entropy":2.931254,"tag_diversity":0.173913,"top_tag_share":0.058528,"avg_upvotes":4.080268,"median_upvotes":2.0,"avg_comments":0.036789,"comment_to_upvote_ratio":0.009422,"zero_engagement_share":0.287625,"viral_share":0.003344,"posts_per_week":2.085051,"non_article_ratio":0.0,"author_present_share":0.0,"recency_skew":0.073609},"view_coords":{"engagement_style":[3.4265,-5.9118],"cadence_depth":[9.2206,-8.0588],"hype_variety":[1.7206,-2.9265],"title_style":[-3.7941,-8.6618]},"top_tags":[["spring",439],["java",418],["apache",84],["spring-boot",83],["cpra",82],["security",81],["vmware",80],["microservices",77]],"sample_titles":{"representative":["Null-Safe applications with Spring Boot 4","Spring Boot 3.5.10 available now","Bootiful Spring Boot in 2024 (part 1)"],"outlier":["A Bootiful Podcast: S\u00e9bastien Deleuze on Spring Framework and Kotlin, GraalVM, Project Leyden, AppCDS, runtime efficiency, Kotlin, and more"]},"recent_posts":[{"id":"wGVpJp3mq","title":"Blending Chat with Rich UIs with Spring AI and MCP Apps","url":"https://spring.io/blog/2026/03/18/mcp-apps","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/blending-chat-with-rich-uis-with-spring-ai-and-mcp-apps-wgvpjp3mq","summary":"Spring AI 2.0.0-M3 introduces MCP Apps, a way to embed rich HTML/JavaScript UIs directly inside AI chat interfaces. Using @McpResource and @McpTool annotations on a Spring Boot MCP server, developers can serve interactive UI components (like a dice roller) that communicate bidirectionally with the AI assistant host via JSON-RPC. The ext-apps.ts module enables the UI to update the model context, send messages, and call server tools. The tutorial walks through project setup, defining the HTML UI, implementing the MCP server, configuring Streamable HTTP transport, and testing with clients like Claude Desktop or MCP Jam.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/ff749d548af41095da8724da8d7ba5f9?_a=AQAEuop","num_upvotes":2,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2026-03-18T00:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"ahkqogF9O","title":"Moving beyond Strings in Spring Data","url":"https://spring.io/blog/2026/02/27/moving-beyond-strings-in-spring-data","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/moving-beyond-strings-in-spring-data-ahkqogf9o","summary":"Spring Data 2026.0.0-M1 introduces type-safe property paths as an alternative to string-based property references in queries. String-based references lack compiler validation and IDE refactoring support, causing bugs that only surface at runtime. The new approach uses Java method references (e.g., TypedPropertyPath.of(Person::getFirstName)) and Kotlin property references with operator overloads, providing compile-time validation, IDE navigation, and refactoring safety. Existing string-based APIs remain fully supported; type-safe paths are strictly additive and can be adopted incrementally. Method references are introspected once and cached for performance.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/ff749d548af41095da8724da8d7ba5f9?_a=AQAEuop","num_upvotes":22,"num_comments":1,"created_at":"2026-02-27T00:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"8TEF3jM08","title":"This Week in Spring - February 24th, 2026","url":"https://spring.io/blog/2026/02/24/this-week-in-spring-february-24th-2026","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/this-week-in-spring---february-24th-2026-8tef3jm08","summary":"A weekly roundup of news and updates from the Spring ecosystem, covering Java, Spring Boot, cloud, microservices, and related topics.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/ff749d548af41095da8724da8d7ba5f9?_a=AQAEuop","num_upvotes":1,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2026-02-24T00:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"mjkSTeKZ8","title":"Spring Boot 3.5.11 available now","url":"https://spring.io/blog/2026/02/19/spring-boot-3-5-11-available-now","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/spring-boot-3-5-11-available-now-mjkstekz8","summary":"Spring Boot 3.5.11 has been released. This is a maintenance release in the 3.5.x line, available now from the Spring project under Broadcom.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/ff749d548af41095da8724da8d7ba5f9?_a=AQAEuop","num_upvotes":18,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2026-02-19T00:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"4wdP32pyI","title":"Spring Boot 4.0.3 available now","url":"https://spring.io/blog/2026/02/19/spring-boot-4-0-3-available-now","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/spring-boot-4-0-3-available-now-4wdp32pyi","summary":"Spring Boot 4.0.3 has been released. This is a maintenance release in the 4.0.x line, available now from the Spring project at Broadcom.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/ff749d548af41095da8724da8d7ba5f9?_a=AQAEuop","num_upvotes":44,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2026-02-19T00:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"z05vc76B3","title":"Spring Framework 7.0.5 Available Now","url":"https://spring.io/blog/2026/02/18/spring-framework-7-0-5-available-now","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/spring-framework-7-0-5-available-now-z05vc76b3","summary":"Spring Framework 7.0.5 has been released. No further details are available from the content.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/ff749d548af41095da8724da8d7ba5f9?_a=AQAEuop","num_upvotes":35,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2026-02-18T00:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"ezsCJ6WeK","title":"Spring for Apache Pulsar 1.2.15 and 2.0.3 are now availab